@startuml clnrm-v1.3.0-test-execution-sequence
title Sequence Diagram - Full Test Execution with Live-Check (v1.3.0)

actor Developer
participant "CLI" as CLI
participant "Core" as Core
participant "WeaverController" as Weaver
participant "OTEL SDK" as OTEL
participant "TestEnvironment" as Env
participant "Docker Backend" as Docker
participant "Weaver Process" as WeaverProc
participant "Validation Engine" as Validator

Developer -> CLI: clnrm run tests/ --validate

' Initialization phase
CLI -> Core: parse TOML config
Core -> Core: load [weaver] section
Core -> Weaver: new(WeaverConfig)

' Weaver startup (Weaver-first pattern)
CLI -> Weaver: start_and_coordinate()
activate Weaver

Weaver -> Weaver: cleanup_orphaned_processes()
note right: pkill -9 -f "weaver registry live-check"

Weaver -> Weaver: find_available_port_with_fallback()
note right: Try 4317-4327, fallback 5317-5327, 6317-6337

Weaver -> WeaverProc: spawn process
activate WeaverProc
note right
    weaver registry live-check \
      --registry registry/ \
      --otlp-grpc-port 4317 \
      --admin-port 8080 \
      --format json \
      --output validation_output/
end note

Weaver -> WeaverProc: health_check_with_timeout(30s)
loop Exponential backoff (100ms → 1000ms)
    Weaver -> WeaverProc: GET http://localhost:8080/health
    WeaverProc --> Weaver: 200 OK
end

Weaver --> CLI: WeaverCoordination\n{pid, otlp_port, admin_port}
deactivate Weaver

' OTEL initialization
CLI -> OTEL: init_otel(OtelConfig)
note right
    endpoint: http://localhost:4317
    exporter: OTLP gRPC
    sample_ratio: 1.0
end note
activate OTEL

' Test execution phase
CLI -> Core: execute_tests()
activate Core

Core -> Env: CleanroomEnvironment::new()
activate Env

Env -> Docker: create_container("postgres:15-alpine")
activate Docker
Docker --> Env: container_id
deactivate Docker

Core -> OTEL: emit span("test.execute")
note right
    Attributes:
    - test.name
    - test.hermetic
    - container.id
    - test.result
end note
OTEL -> WeaverProc: OTLP gRPC stream
WeaverProc -> WeaverProc: validate against schema
note right: Real-time validation

Core -> Env: execute_scenario("api_with_database")
Env -> Docker: exec_in_container(["my-api", "--endpoint", "/api/v1/users"])
Docker --> Env: output
Env -> OTEL: emit span("http.server.request")
OTEL -> WeaverProc: OTLP stream
Env -> OTEL: emit span("db.query", parent="http.server.request")
OTEL -> WeaverProc: OTLP stream

Env -> Docker: cleanup_containers()
Docker --> Env: cleanup complete
deactivate Env

Core --> CLI: test results
deactivate Core

' OTEL flush
CLI -> OTEL: drop(_guard)
deactivate OTEL
note right: Flush pending telemetry

CLI -> CLI: sleep(500ms)
note right: Ensure all telemetry delivered

' Weaver shutdown and validation
CLI -> Weaver: stop_and_report()
activate Weaver

Weaver -> WeaverProc: SIGHUP signal
note right: Graceful shutdown

WeaverProc -> WeaverProc: generate validation report
WeaverProc --> Weaver: exit(0)
deactivate WeaverProc

Weaver -> Weaver: parse validation_report.json
Weaver -> Validator: analyze_violations()
activate Validator

Validator -> Validator: check sample_count > 0
note right: CRITICAL: Zero samples = FAILURE

Validator -> Validator: check violations == 0
Validator -> Validator: check coverage >= threshold
Validator --> Weaver: ValidationReport\n{status, violations, coverage}
deactivate Validator

Weaver --> CLI: ValidationReport
deactivate Weaver

' Exit code determination
alt Violations > 0
    CLI -> CLI: exit(1)
    CLI --> Developer: ❌ Validation failed\n(violations detected)
else Sample count == 0
    CLI -> CLI: exit(1)
    CLI --> Developer: ❌ Validation failed\n(no telemetry received)
else Success
    CLI -> CLI: exit(0)
    CLI --> Developer: ✅ Validation passed
end

note over Developer, WeaverProc
    **Weaver-First Pattern (v1.3.0):**
    1. Start Weaver BEFORE tests (get coordination)
    2. Configure OTEL to target Weaver's actual port
    3. Run tests (emit telemetry to Weaver)
    4. Flush OTEL (ensure delivery)
    5. Stop Weaver (get validation report)
    6. Fail if violations OR zero samples

    **Critical Principle:**
    Zero samples = broken test, not passing test.
    Prevents false positives from tests that don't emit telemetry.
end note

@enduml

